    ("gov_m5_45", "International Organizations: UN Trusteeship Council", "2013", "The United Nations Trusteeship Council was established to:", ["Supervise the administration of trust territories transitioning to self-government or independence", "Manage global currency reserves", "Collect taxes from sovereign states", "Control nuclear power plants"], 0, "The Trusteeship Council oversaw the transition of 11 trust territories (such as Tanganyika and British Cameroons) to independence.", "Easy"),
    ("gov_m5_46", "International Organizations: Commonwealth Sanctions on Nigeria", "2010", "Nigeria was suspended from the Commonwealth of Nations in November 1995 following the:", ["Execution of Ken Saro-Wiwa and eight other Ogoni environmental activists by the Abacha military regime", "Annexation of the Bakassi Peninsula", "Cancellation of foreign debt repayments", "Boycott of the Olympic Games"], 0, "The Auckland Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (CHOGM) suspended Nigeria over human rights violations and summary executions of the Ogoni 9.", "Easy"),
